  "answer": "A synapse is the functional region of contact between two neurons, where information from one neuron is transmitted or relayed to another neuron. The transfer of information across a synapse occurs through either chemical or electrical signals, or both. When an electrical impulse reaches the end of an axon, it triggers the release of chemical messengers called neurotransmitters. These neurotransmitters cross the synapse and bind to receptors on the dendrites of the next neuron, thereby transmitting the signal.",
